def main():
 old=(O/'report_before_review3.md').read_text();r=load(P/'20261108_preflight/technical_progress.json');d=load(O/'e1_stratified_design.json');w=load(O/'e1_interval_width.json');b=load(O/'baseline_diagnostics.json');c=load(O/'cost_projection.json');cost=load(P/'20261108_preflight/costs.json')
 s='# Batch-1 pilot report — review 3, 2026-11-08\n\nAll five reserved-ID technical pilots completed; overall review verdict remains **FAIL**. No full batch runs, commits or protected-file edits. Human validation and proposed settings remain unfrozen.\n\n'
 s+=table(['Experiment','Decision','What blocks it'],[['E1','GO schema pilot; FIX design freeze','Plan A and stratified draw pending; no tested size reaches ±0.10 fidelity κ precision under planning assumptions; human labels absent.'],['E4','FIX','Donor re-pilot improves 6/15 → 7/15 matched controls; selection clarification pending and most cases have only one eligible donor.'],['E4-P','GO technical','Seed 43 approved and enabled for the full-run config; final targets still depend on human validation.'],['E2-C','FIX','Strict R1 invalidity 5/10 (missing mode names); casebook references remain provisional.'],['E2-A','FIX','Strict R1 invalidity 11/20; W&W step abstains 7/20; no human-qualified kept injections.']])
 s+='## E1: interval-width design, not acceptance thresholds\n\nThe κ/accuracy acceptance thresholds are removed. The rebuttal reports estimates and 95% CIs only. `prereg/E1.md` now fully specifies proposed fact-level presence/fidelity primaries, trace-level binary secondaries, lexical sampling, inclusion probabilities, weights and fixed IDs for 60, 80 and 100 held-out instances. These are **planned, pending author confirmation**; no sample enlargement or matcher freeze has occurred.\n\n'
 s+=table(['Lexical τ = 0.5 stratum','Frame N','Draw 60','Draw 80','Draw 100'],[[h,len(ids)]+[d['designs'][str(n)]['strata'][h]['target'] for n in [60,80,100]] for h,ids in d['ordered_strata'].items()])
 s+='The frame excludes 20 fixed dev instances, leaving 85 MuSiQue and 47 Silo-Bench instances. Strata use only cached Qwen k = 3 lexical coverage: zero, incomplete, complete. Neither correctness nor matcher output selects IDs. Within strata, fixed SHA ordering uses `["E1-lexical-v3", 42, stratum, instance_id]`. Inclusion probability is **πₕ = nₕ/Nₕ**, weight **wᵢ = Nₕ/nₕ**; all model/fact rows inherit the instance weight. The full ID lists and exact weights are in the prereg and `20261108_review3/e1_stratified_design.json`.\n\n'
 s+='The analysis script `src/audit/e1_weighted_analysis.py` reports weighted human κ and matcher accuracy for fact presence and fidelity, separately; 2,000 bootstrap draws resample whole instances within lexical strata. Board is the primary checkpoint; extraction is separate. Failed machine labels remain errors. Trace binary primary excludes partial/uncertain with counts; sensitivity counts partial as lost, still excludes uncertain. **Human labels do not exist yet, so whether these analyses change conclusions is not known.** Both will be reported.\n\n'
 s+='Named outputs **`MQ_candidate_aggregation_failure_rate_human`** and **`SB_candidate_aggregation_failure_rate_human`** directly address the 68% headline. Denominator: all traces, including correct answers; numerator: wrong traces with a human-validated faithfully complete support set on the board. Pooled and per-model estimates include the 20 dev instances as human-labelled certainty units; validation statistics exclude them. The script refuses a full-frame rate without those dev labels. It also reports an unresolved-case upper sensitivity; no model-derived label substitutes for a human reference.\n\n'
 s+='### Expected 95% CI half-widths\n\nEach cell is κ / accuracy half-width. Central setting: true κ = 0.75, accuracy = 0.85; brackets give the range over κ = 0.70–0.80 and accuracy = 0.85–0.90. Instance ICC = 0.25; 200 simulated panels per cell, each with 2,000 bootstrap draws. Lexical τ = 0.5 provides the presence/trace split. Gold support-unit count is a conservative proxy for atomic-fact count.\n\n'
 rows=[]
 for n in ['original60','60','80','100']:
  cells=[]
  for metric,fp in [('presence',None),('fidelity',.85),('fidelity',.95),('trace',None)]:
   rr=[x for x in w['results'] if x['design']==n and x['metric']==metric and x['faithful_fraction_assumption']==fp];mid=next(x for x in rr if x['true_kappa']==.75 and x['true_accuracy']==.85)
   cells.append(f"{mid['mean_kappa_half_width']:.3f} / {mid['mean_accuracy_half_width']:.3f} [{min(x['mean_kappa_half_width'] for x in rr):.3f}–{max(x['mean_kappa_half_width'] for x in rr):.3f} / {min(x['mean_accuracy_half_width'] for x in rr):.3f}–{max(x['mean_accuracy_half_width'] for x in rr):.3f}]")
  rows.append([n]+cells)
 s+=table(['Held-out draw','Fact presence','Fact fidelity: 85% faithful','Fact fidelity: 95% faithful','Trace binary'],rows)
 s+='Lexical coverage **cannot identify fidelity prevalence**. The 85%/95% faithful splits are sensitivity assumptions, with remaining mass 90% partial and 10% distorted; they are not observed labels. Joint carrier groups are collapsed to one fidelity call per atomic fact using the prereg rule. The simulation models one fact per gold support unit, three model traces, no uncertain exclusions and no finite-population correction; more exclusions or different atomic granularity change precision. `e1_interval_width.json` contains all scenarios and undefined-κ frequencies. The old 10/85 split came from the historical low-threshold labels; it is not reused for the new τ = 0.5 draw.\n\n'
 s+=table(['Held-out N','Held-out annotation h','Per annotator h','Extra vs 60','Total E1 h including unchanged dev budget'],[[n,f"{w['hours'][str(n)]['total_held_out_hours']:.1f}",f"{w['hours'][str(n)]['per_annotator']:.2f}",f"{w['hours'][str(n)]['extra_vs_60']:.1f}",f"{112+w['hours'][str(n)]['extra_vs_60']:.1f}"] for n in [60,80,100]])
 s+='Hours assume two passes over three model traces (7 minutes each on MQ, 20 on SB), plus 0.55 h per instance for fact specification/adjudication. Calibration remains separate. **Recommendation: none of 60/80/100 meets ±0.10 on both primary statistics once fidelity κ is included.** Presence alone is near the target at 80; at 100 fidelity κ still has central half-width 0.134–0.195. Keep 60 as the unexpanded planning budget while authors confirm Plan A and review the fidelity prevalence/granularity assumptions; do not describe 100 as adequately precise. No larger population was invented or sampled.\n\n'
 s+='### E1 technical matcher result retained\n\n`semantic-dev-v2` remains unfrozen: strict schema; at most two retries per logical call; every attempt logged; only whitespace/one complete JSON fence tolerated, never repaired labels. Same five reserved IDs and 30 traces: **0/30 failed, 0/60 logical calls retried**. Each base-model × k cell is 0/5 failed (Qwen-235B, GPT-4o-mini, Gemma-4-31B; k = 1 and 3), Qwen judge throughout. Prompt+retry hash: `3d97341d410e0d2e93df919a28af59c7e2d389751ae43f6eb5258038f8ddc57c`. Full initial inventory remains **1,976 calls**: 1,824 matcher + 152 GPT prerequisites. Measured 60 matcher calls cost $0.018822 and 263.5 API seconds; projected matcher-only cost $0.57 / 2.22 serial API hours, versus $1.23 at the 2k-token planning assumption.\n\n'
 s+='## Baseline validity and strict/code-only scoring\n\n`prereg/Baseline-scoring-v3.md` fixes strict primary (invalid = wrong, retained denominator) and code-only sensitivity, planned pending confirmation for final evaluation. Current pilot rescoring is retrospective diagnostics. Released prompts and taxonomy are unchanged. The sensitivity accepts a valid mode code without its name only when agent and step are valid; it never changes a code or fills a label. W&W step-by-step uses its actual released stopping rule and native zero-based coordinate.\n\n'
 rows=[]
 for x in b['settings']:
  method,model,bench,exp=x['setting'];rows.append([exp,bench,method,model.split('/')[-1],f"{x['strict_invalid']}/{x['n']} ({x['strict_invalid']/x['n']:.0%})",(f"{x['code_only_invalid']}/{x['n']}" if method=='r1' else 'not applicable'),'; '.join(f'{k}: {v}' for k,v in x['causes'].items()) or 'none'])
