 external=external.replace('Batch-2 dependency; do not silently omit or substitute gold supports','Both proxy paths technically piloted; dev choice remains unfrozen. No gold-support substitution')
 s+=external
 s+='## E4 donor controls\n\nOriginal 6/15 matches: nine failures comprise **five shorter controls, three longer controls and one donor with no unused next unit**. Eight of those nine failing pairs have only one eligible donor; the remaining case has two. Examples: repair/control tokens 65/58 (10.8% short), 49/66 (34.7% long), 33/0 (no next unit). Donor eligibility is preserved: other board agents, prefer support-free agents, existing fallback when none are support-free. No eligibility is inferred from an answer outcome.\n\n'
 s+='Proposed clarification: among eligible donors, prefer the same added-unit count, then the closest exact-base-token total; break ties by SHA-256 of `[42, instance_id, arm, donor_agent]`. Keep the original next-unit score order and verbatim-source-span rule. Do not pad, shorten, change the ±10% rule, or call a mismatched pair matched. This is **planned, pending author confirmation** for the full run.\n\n'
 s+='The requested same-ID technical re-pilot is complete: **7/15 matched**, up from 6/15. One extraction control changes from 74/64 to 74/79 tokens; the other eight failures remain. All three controls on each of five reserved items were re-evaluated; identical outcomes were reused. Only **2 new calls**, **$0.000231**, **4.30 API seconds** were needed. Each donor/action choice was saved before the new answer. Changed-source fidelity remains an author check; E4 stays FIX. Artifacts: `20261108_e4_donor_v2/`.\n\n'
 s+='## E2-A kept-injection yield\n\nThe $22.70 measured projection is a **200-candidate technical workload**, not 200 kept injections; it runs baselines even for unkept cases. For the yield calculation only, assume 50 candidates per fault type (not a changed config). The pilot is too small and lacks author screening/postchecks, so it cannot establish human-qualified yield.\n\n'
 y=load(O/'e2a_yield.json');rows=[]
 for kind in ['extraction_omission','selection_omission','distortion','aggregation']:
  rr=[x for x in y if x['type']==kind];raw=sum(x['raw_provisional_keep'] for x in rr);kept=sum(x['keep'] for x in rr)
  rows.append([kind,len(rr),f'{raw}/{len(rr)}',f'{kept}/{len(rr)}',f'{50*kept/len(rr):.0f}', 'not estimable; human checks absent'])
 s+=table(['Fault type','Pilot candidates','Original provisional keep','Conservative single-defect pass','Projected pass / 50 candidates','Human-qualified kept yield'],rows)
 s+='The original extraction rate was 1/2, which would suggest 25/50 candidates; its postcheck shows additional missing facts, so it is not a single-defect keep. The conservative technical point projection is therefore 0 for each type, **not evidence that the true human-screened yield is zero**. With only 0/2 or 0/1, Wilson 95% upper rates are about 66%/79% (33/40 per 50 candidates). “Up to 30 per fault type” is a cap, not a demonstrated attainable yield. Aggregation additionally awaits the human visible-step check. A code-review fix accepts the actual `extraction_omission`/`selection_omission` names in the keep predicate; raw outputs were not changed.\n\n'
 s+='## Approved seed 43 and updated budgets\n\nSeed 43 is **on** in `rebuttal/configs/E4-P-full.json`; pilot configs are unchanged. This is a planning config, not authorisation to execute a full run now. Seed-43 outcomes are clustered by underlying task across seeds. The one-item pilot is discarded for final inference and the full run makes fresh calls. Option (b) remains dropped because the paper has no second benchmark with established extraction and distortion groups.\n\n'
 rows=[]
 for exp in ['E1','E4','E4-P','E2-C','E2-A']:
  plan=cost['experiments'][exp];projection=c['projection'][exp];rows.append([exp,f"{plan['calls']:,}",f"${plan['usd']:.2f}",f"{projection['calls']:,.0f}",f"${projection['usd']:.2f}",plan['annotation_hours']])
 rows.append(['**Batch 1**',f"**{c['planned']['calls']:,}**",f"**${c['planned']['usd']:.2f}**",f"**{c['total_excluding_proxy']['calls']:,.0f}**",f"**${c['total_excluding_proxy']['usd']:.2f}**",'**154 h; ≈9 days**'])
 s+=table(['Experiment','Planned calls','Planned USD','Pilot-projected calls','Pilot-projected USD','Annotation h'],rows)
 s+='The technical E6 proxy supplement adds 1,400 projected calls / $0.46 for 200 candidates: total **26,370 / $31.74** including it. E4-P includes the approved 78 extra seed-43 traces: planned 4,368 calls / $5.59 / 4 h; one-item measured projection 4,368 calls / $2.41. Expected added groups remain cache projections (extraction ≈16, selection ≈40, aggregation ≈12, strict distortion ≈0–1), not new-seed outcomes.\n\n'
 s+='Prices: OpenRouter route, [saved provider metadata](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models), checked 2026-11-08. Input/output USD per million: Qwen 0.14/0.80, GPT-4o-mini 0.15/0.60, Gemma 0.20/0.40, Gemini 0.75/3.75. Planned estimates assume 70/30 input/output and 2k tokens per baseline/judge call, original cohort weights 300 MQ/63 SB5/63 SB10. Measured projections use actual ledger token/call mix; E1’s 152 GPT prerequisites remain an explicit $0.04 estimate. E2-A’s plan assumes about 120 kept injections, whereas its technical projection spends on all 200 candidates. Thus the cost columns are workload scenarios, not like-for-like expected efficacy budgets. Screening, retries, new source populations and changed E1 design can add work. No unapproved E1 enlargement is included. Calculators: `recompute_costs.py`, `scripts/project_batch1_costs.py`.\n\n'
 s+='## Final external sanity checks\n\n**[R1]: structural check, not a numerical reproduction.** The Gemma variant could not be confirmed as Gemma-4-31B. Five own ALFWorld traces, Qwen-235B, released prompt/taxonomy unchanged: 5/5 agent-step-mode parses, 5/5 in-range steps, 5/5 valid codes, 4/5 valid code+name pairs. Parse-failure rate 0%; strict invalidity 20% due to one missing name.\n\n'
 ww=r['ww_sanity']['evaluation'];s+=f"**Who&When finished: 368/368 conditions**, 184 released native traces × with/without gold, GPT-4o-mini, pinned released all-at-once code. PID 73598 exited; no second worker was started. Native released-evaluator pooled agent accuracy **{ww['agent']:.2%}**, step **{ww['step']:.2%}**; parse success **{ww['parse']:.0%}**. Strict-equality sensitivity: agent **{ww['agent_exact']:.2%}**, step **{ww['step_exact']:.2%}**.\n\n"
 s+=table(['System','Gold answer','Agent accuracy','Step accuracy','N'],[[x['system'],x['gold'],f"{x['agent']:.2%}",f"{x['step']:.2%}",x['n']] for x in ww['cells']])
 s+=f"Against [Who&When, arXiv:2505.00212v3](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.00212), Figure 3’s approximate 55% agent / 4% step values, pooled differences are **{ww['agent']*100-55:+.2f} / {ww['step']*100-4:+.2f} percentage points**. This is a numerical sanity reproduction attempt, not exact agreement. The radar chart lacks exact numeric labels (visual reading roughly ±2 points); OpenRouter versus historical Azure deployment, unknown historical model revision and ambiguous figure aggregation limit comparison. The native evaluator uses substring matching; exact step equality drops the measured step rate to 6.52%. Equal weighting of the four system/gold cells gives 54.11% agent / 8.24% step, further showing aggregation sensitivity.\n\n"
 s+='## Annotation and verification\n\nAnnotation packages remain under `rebuttal/annotation/`: E1 reach/fidelity; nonblind E2-A author screening and postchecks; E4 40 matcher spot checks and swaps; blind E2-B guidelines for batch 2. Each includes a schema, five synthetic worked examples and sheets. Five disjoint calibration source traces exist; **human calibration has not happened**, so no human agreement is claimed. Provisional pilot labels/baseline outputs never enter annotator sheets.\n\nE1 A+B / C+D rotate by instance, with the complementary pair assigned to blind Part B. Recursive allowlist export hides all audit, matcher, lexical and baseline outputs. Current main-study hours per annotator: E1 28, E2-A 7.5, E4 2, approved seed spot checks 1 = 38.5; Part B later 17.5; calibration reserve 2.1 extra. Human calibration statistics remain κ for E1 presence/fidelity/binary, E2-A eligibility/keep, E4 fidelity/swap validity, and Part B class/reference.\n\nFull `.conda-env/bin/python -m pytest -q`: **283 passed** (`20261108_review3/pytest.log`). Added checks cover weighted estimators, stratified instance bootstrap, fixed SHA lists/weights, partial sensitivity and all-trace rate denominator, strict/code-only scoring, W&W abstention, donor tie-breaking, omission-name keep gates and full/pilot config isolation.\n\n'
 s+='## Settings changes for approval\n\n| Proposed setting | Status and plain-language change |\n|---|---|\n| E1 primary unit and draw | **Planned, pending author confirmation:** make fact-level presence/fidelity primary, keep trace-level binary secondary; use the specified lexical τ = 0.5 stratified held-out draw and inverse-probability weights. Sizes 80/100 are alternatives only; none currently meets the fidelity precision goal. |\n| Partial-as-lost sensitivity | **Planned, pending author confirmation:** primary binary excludes partial/uncertain; an additional analysis counts partial as lost while still excluding uncertain. |\n| R1 scoring | **Planned, pending author confirmation:** strict primary counts invalid output wrong; code-only sensitivity accepts a valid code without its name, preserving valid agent/step requirements. Report changes in conclusions. |\n| E4 donor selection | **Planned, pending author confirmation:** among eligible donors choose the closest token total with matching unit count and fixed SHA tie-break, replacing “first other agent”; retain ±10%. Reserved technical re-pilot completed. |\n| Renderer | No change proposed: no input-side defect established. Any future renderer change remains **planned, pending author confirmation** until specified, versioned and re-piloted. |\n\nThe old CI thresholds are removed, not held for approval. Seed 43 is approved and enabled, not a hold. Exact tokenizers and the R1 structural check are completed implementation, not holds.\n\n## Author decisions and recommended defaults\n\nKeep D1 = A and D11 = A. Confirm Plan A and its estimands/weights before labelling or freezing; do not enlarge to a size that does not meet the stated fidelity precision goal. Keep strict baseline scores primary and show code-only sensitivity prominently; do not infer superiority from the invalid-output burden. Keep E4 FIX while controls remain unmatched; do not relax token tolerance. Treat 30 injections per fault type as an unverified cap until human screening and single-defect checks establish yield. No full runs are authorised by this report.\n\n'
